      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is well above the maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Requested dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** The maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Many clinicians cap it at 2,000 mg/day. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The requested dose is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm and give a short rationale for the order note. I'll enter it once I have your answer."
      }
